<BaseLayout title="What to Expect | Healing the Heart">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="page-hero-inner"><p class="eyebrow">Before you begin</p><h1>What to expect</h1><p>If opening up feels intimidating, that makes sense. We want you to know what kind of space you are stepping into.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="content-grid"><article class="content-card"><span class="num">01</span><h3>A safe, confidential atmosphere</h3><p>The goal is compassion, trust, honesty, and freedom from judgment.</p></article><article class="content-card"><span class="num">02</span><h3>Teaching that gives language to pain</h3><p>You will explore the heart, emotional needs, loss, forgiveness, rejection, trust, and restoration.</p></article><article class="content-card"><span class="num">03</span><h3>Personal participation</h3><p>Reading, workbook exercises, Digging Deeper questions, reflection, journaling, prayer, and review are part of the process.</p></article><article class="content-card"><span class="num">04</span><h3>Small-group ministry</h3><p>Healing is not meant to happen in isolation. Honest participation and safe relationships are important parts of the journey.</p></article></div></section>
<section class="dark-section section"><div class="rich-section"><p class="eyebrow light">A gentle reminder</p><h2>You don't have to have it all figured out before you come.</h2><p>You do not need to minimize your pain because someone else had it worse. You do not need to pretend you are already okay. Come honestly, and take the next step from where you are.</p></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
